{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself spices.</b> And what are they? נטף and שחלת etc. But the סמים mentioned afterward are not counted among the spices; rather, it is 'spices' that he already mentioned. And so is the way of the verses — states a general term, then specifies, and goes back and says, 'Here is the general category that I stated.' This is its plain sense. But the words of truth are eternal." "<b>Bad be-vad it shall be.</b> Each one prepared on its own in equal weight — unlike the other fragrant spices — and afterward they are mixed together."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:19.746165555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}